%% The portfolio is a read and has no state of its own. What changes is how one Property
%% appears in it for one viewer. Every arrow is a command of ANOTHER feature, named, because
%% the portfolio never causes any of them and re-reads on every request (no cross-request cache).
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Absent: Property created, viewer holds no reach

  Absent --> Withheld: assign Property to the Staff Member (analytics off)
  Absent --> Operational: assign Property to the Staff Member (analytics on)
  Withheld --> Operational: enable analytics for the Property
  Operational --> Withheld: disable analytics for the Property
  Operational --> Full: grant finance.manage_folio
  Full --> Operational: revoke finance.manage_folio
  Withheld --> Absent: unassign Property from the Staff Member
  Operational --> Absent: unassign Property from the Staff Member
  Full --> Absent: unassign Property from the Staff Member
  Absent --> [*]: archive Property
  Withheld --> [*]: archive Property
  Operational --> [*]: archive Property
  Full --> [*]: archive Property

  note right of Absent
    No row, and nothing says a row was left out.
    Also the state for every suspended or cancelled Subscription.
  end note
  note right of Withheld
    Row present, name only, every figure null.
  end note
  note right of Operational
    Counts shown, money null.
  end note
  note right of Full
    Counts and money shown.
  end note
